design.simIntegration:
Every hook is ONE branch reading a cached scalar inside a loop/aggregate that already runs — no new pass, no new per-tile iteration, asymptotics unchanged. With all ordinances off, every mul=1 / additive=0, so output is byte-identical to today (verifiable by diffing a paused city's overlays before/after the patch).

1. POLLUTION — recomputeMaps() src accumulation (sim.js line 763-766). Apply recycle mul to the two curbside sources only (plant flue smog untouched — recycling is waste, not combustion):
   const pm = this.ordMods.pollMul;
   if (t===OV.ZI) src[i] += (30 + this.lvl[i]*35) * pm;
   if (t===OV.ROAD || t===OV.WIREROAD) src[i] += 8 * pm;
   diffuse()+clamp unchanged; cleaner air also lifts downwind land value for free via existing land-value pass.

2. CRIME — recomputeMaps() crime loop (line 807). crimeCut is additive flat, behaving like extra police coverage, strongest where density outruns thin coverage:
   const v = density - this.polCov[i] - this.landv[i]*0.2 - this.ordMods.crimeCut;
   existing Math.max(0,min(255,v)) at 808 bounds it.

3. TRAFFIC — recomputeTraffic() trip emission (line ~669, inside the per-zone loop that computes trips). Scale at the source so fewer trips deposit everywhere the walk lands, no 2nd pass:
   const trips = (4 + this.lvl[i]*9) * this.ordMods.trafficMul;   // if 'trips' is not the current local name, multiply the existing trip-count expression
   Lower congestion feeds back through growthPass cong-damping and the trafficNear land-value penalty — a satisfying 2nd-order boost to growth/values.

4. DEMAND — recomputeDemand() (line 882-884). Fold ordMods deltas into the SAME additive slot the time-capsule event mods use (evR/evC/evI), so they compose and clamp identically:
   this.demand.r = clampD(jobsAvail/220 + taxMod + stadMod + svcMod + evR + this.ordMods.demR);
   this.demand.c = clampD((pop*0.28 - cJobs)/160 + taxMod*0.6 + svcMod*0.5 + evC + this.ordMods.demC);
   this.demand.i = clampD((pop*0.42 - iJobs)/180 + 0.28 + taxMod*0.4 + svcMod*0.5 + evI + this.ordMods.demI);
   Also cache commercial jobs for the tax: at line 869 add this.comJobs = cJobs; (this.jobs already = cJobs+iJobs). recomputeDemand runs every tick before the monthly collectBudget, so pop/comJobs are current at rollover.

5. FIRE — fireTick() burnout (line 944). Smoke detectors add to the decrement, same shape as the coverage bonus:
   this.fire[i] = Math.max(0, this.fire[i] - 1 - (cov>40?2:0) - this.ordMods.fireBurn);

6. BUDGET — new O(1) helper ordinanceBudget() over the 6-entry table using cached this.pop/comJobs plus one count of resTiles (fold resTiles into deptCosts' existing single map pass, which already counts roads/wires/stations, and stash this.resTiles — no new scan):
   ordinanceBudget(){ let cost=0,rev=0; for(const o of ORDINANCES){ if(!this.ordinances[o.id]||this.tier<o.minTier) continue; if(o.cost) cost+=o.cost(this); if(o.revenue) rev+=o.revenue(this);} return {cost,rev,net:rev-cost}; }
   In collectBudget() (line 1166): const ob=this.ordinanceBudget(); const net = taxes - roadCost - serviceCost - plantCost - debt + ob.net; and add to lastBudget: {..., ord: ob.net, ordCost: ob.cost, ordRev: ob.rev}. updateRecords/City-Hall net (recCur.net) picks it up automatically since it reads lastBudget.net. deptCosts() itself is untouched (ordinances aren't a department); the budget dialog gets one dedicated "City Ordinances" line via fillBudgetTable() reading lastBudget.ord.

7. TOGGLE + LOAD — the dialog checkbox handler (bound once in bindDialogs, delegated on .ord-check like .fund-slider) calls city.enactOrdinance(id,checked), then recomputeMaps()+recomputeTraffic()+recomputeDemand() so crime/pollution/traffic overlays and demand react within a frame EVEN WHILE PAUSED; Snd.click on success, Snd.denied if locked; then re-renders the row cost cells + footer net. deserialize() calls recomputeOrdinances() before the existing recompute cascade (line 1426) so ordMods is warm when those run.

ADVISORS (advisors.js, M23 bias). Shared helper adviseOrdinances(champion): for each ORDINANCES entry with matching champion and city.tier>=minTier — if enacted → one self-congratulatory in-voice line; else if the advisor's live metric crosses a threshold → one recommend line citing the number and pointing at the Ordinances panel. Thresholds reuse existing aggregates (no new scan): watch/curfew via advAvg(city.crime)>=45; recycle via advAvg(city.poll)>=45; carpool via advRoadTraffic()>=70; nostalgiaTax via city.funds<800; smoke via advAvg(city.fireCov)<48. Push via out.push(...adviseOrdinances(DEPT_CHAMPION-equivalent key)) inside adviseSafety/adviseEnvironment/adviseTransport/adviseFinance next to the existing deptFundingLine calls. THE BIAS IS THE FUN: each advisor over-sells its own ordinance ignoring cross-department cost — Finance pushes the Nostalgia Tax even as it kneecaps commercial demand; Safety pushes Curfew ignoring the same commerce hit; Environment pushes Recycling regardless of the § cost. Recs self-suppress once enacted (off-gate), no nag loop; they ride the existing ADV_REACT_TTL/500ms dialog cadence, not per tick.
